  "assessments": {
    "thm-littlewood-richardson-schur-product-expansion": "Checked every numbered step against current full Jacobi–Trudi, skew-tableau expansion, Hall duality, integral Schur basis and stable-generator proofs. The i/i+1 signature deletes matched parentheses, raising changes the last unmatched i+1 and lowering the first unmatched i; both preserve tableau inequalities by the two-row neutral-rectangle reduction, independently corroborated by the complete van Leeuwen Proposition 3.2.1 proof. The transposed determinant gives alpha_i=nu_sigma(i)-sigma(i)+i, so alpha+delta permutes the distinct nu+delta entries. At the first failing prefix, signature (a,b) goes to (b+1,a-1); the first unmatched i+1 stays fixed because at most a-1 raising operations occur, and lowering acts after all unmatched i+1 positions. The earlier prefix is therefore unchanged for all labels, and the same i is selected on reversal. Equality a=b+1 is excluded by distinct shifted entries. Composing sigma on the right by the adjacent transposition swaps the required coordinates and reverses sign. Lattice survivors force decreasing alpha+delta and thus identity sigma/content nu. Hall adjointness establishes both expansions without rectification, confluence, an external normal-form theorem or circular use of LR. Empty skew/factors, d=1, incompatible containment/degree and finite support are covered.",
    "thm-outer-induction-makes-the-graded-representation-group-a-commutative-ring": "Checked full current induction/conjugation and external-tensor helper proofs and the transitivity supplier. The relabeling is the group map c_t(sigma)=beta_t sigma beta_t^-1; pulling an induced function back along c_t preserves right covariance and left translation, including t=0. The three-block subgroup J and its external product character agree in both parenthesizations; finite-index tensor induction and transitivity give associativity. The explicit block swap conjugates the ordered subgroup and transports the representation, giving commutativity. Evaluation at identity and g↦g^-1v give the unit. Bilinear extension uses only finite virtual-character expansions. No point-label map is applied to a group-valued argument and no infinite-index tensor identification is used.",
    "thm-outer-littlewood-richardson-rule": "After completing the Schur LR and characteristic supplier review, checked all four current proof phases. The conjugation group pullback transports covariance, left action, cycle types and the actual Specht polytabloids. The complete characteristic outer-product proof counts invariant cycle unions; the complete Specht-to-Schur proof inverts the integral Kostka matrix, and the isometry gives injectivity. These yield the finite LR character expansion. Equal characters imply isomorphic finite-dimensional complex representations, and the irreducibility/distinctness suppliers identify exactly the stated Specht multiplicities. The positive LR coefficients are finite tableau counts; zero/empty factors and label transport introduce no extra hypotheses.",
    "prop-restriction-coproduct-is-schur-skewing": "After outer LR, checked every current step and full direct-product character-basis, Frobenius reciprocity and tensor-basis supplier proofs. Restriction is pulled back along the exact zero-based block embedding; its coefficient in the orthonormal external-product basis is the reciprocity pairing with the transported outer induction character. Outer LR identifies it with c^lambda_mu,nu. The finite Schur/skew expansion gives the characteristic formula, and the tensor basis isomorphism proves the stated equivalence in reverse. Endpoint coproducts, noncontainment, incompatible size and finite-degree support are explicit. The corrected source locator is corroboration, with no proof supplied by citation alone.",
    "thm-outer-induction-and-restriction-form-a-graded-hopf-algebra": "After the ring, restriction/skewing, connected-antipode and full Mackey suppliers, checked all current proof phases. c_t goes zero-based to one-based and c_t^-1 brings outer blocks back, with valid induced-function transport. Triple block restrictions give coassociativity and endpoints give counits. The source-row/target-column 2x2 matrix has margins (m,n)/(a,b); the increasing representatives classify K\\S_N/H because explicitly constructed k,h satisfy kgh=g_M. The intersection has target order (r,u,s,v); the source restriction order (r,s,u,v) is regrouped before external-factor induction. Summing matrices is exactly every coproduct degree allocation, proving multiplicativity for honest then virtual characters, with zero block sizes allowed. The graded augmentation is multiplicative and degree zero is Z. The recursive antipode supplier proves a two-sided inverse over arbitrary commutative rings without selecting tensor expressions. The tableau X/Y split proves the diagonal coproduct; Delta(h_n)=sum h_i⊗h_j and E(-t)H(t)=1 make T=(-1)^degree omega a two-sided antipode on free h-generators. Multiplicativity of the two convolution maps uses commutativity of Lambda. Characteristic transport and convolution uniqueness give the full Hopf isomorphism.",
    "ex-outer-product-s32-with-s2": "After the complete outer LR/Pieri and standard-polytabloid basis suppliers, checked all current steps. The group conjugation bridge transports blocks, tabloids, column stabilizers/signs and induced functions in the correct direction. Of the six size-seven partitions containing (3,2), only (3,2,1,1) repeats an added column; the five horizontal strips are (5,2),(4,3),(4,2,1),(3,3,1),(3,2,2), each with multiplicity one. The removable-corner recursion gives input dimensions 5,1 and output dimensions 14,14,35,21,21. The coset/subset bijection gives index binomial(7,2)=21, so the induced and output dimensions are both 105. This checks the actual numerical statement and module decomposition, including the relabeling correction."
